 "▼ Dive in: <0>Errors as data</0>": "",
 "Treat tool names and descriptions as part of your prompt: clear names, narrow purpose, explicit arguments and examples help the model choose correctly.": "",
 "Return failures as <0>data</0> (<1/> plus an actionable message) so the model can recover instead of the whole run crashing.": "",
 "Prefer a few narrow tools over one do-everything tool with a <0/> parameter; very large tool sets may also hurt selection (this tends to vary by model).": "",
 "Keep results compact: everything a tool returns is appended to the context and re-sent each turn.": "",
