 "Deepest level reached — next slide → <0>Security: tool results are untrusted data</0>": "",
 "Injection demo": "",
 "Policy table": "",
 "<0>Instructions (you control)</0><1/>system prompt, your tool definitions, the real user's message.": "",
 "<0>Data (anyone may control)</0><1/>web pages, emails, documents, search results, other agents' output - <2>all tool results</2>.": "",
 "Both end up in <0>one token sequence</0>. There is no hardware-enforced boundary between \"instructions\" and \"data\" inside the model. See <1>prompt injection</1>.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Injection demo</0>": "",
 "Everything a tool returns (web pages, emails, files) enters the <0>same token stream</0> as your instructions. The model cannot reliably tell data from commands: that is <1>prompt injection</1>.": "",
 "Design so that even a fooled model cannot do serious harm: <0>least privilege</0>, <1>confirmation for side effects</1>, and no secrets in reach.": "",
 "Labelling or delimiting untrusted content may reduce the chance the model follows it, but is not a guarantee.": "",
 "Treat model output as untrusted too: validate arguments before executing, as with any user input.": "",
