 "Write a tool once as an MCP server; any MCP-capable host can use it.": "",
 "Compare with defining tools directly in your API request (<0>tool definitions</0>): MCP moves the definition and execution into a separate process. Protocol overview alongside skills and agent-to-agent: <1>protocols</1>.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Primitives</0>": "",
 "The Model Context Protocol (MCP) standardizes how an AI application connects to <0>tools, resources and prompts</0> provided by separate servers, instead of writing custom glue for each tool.": "",
 "It is a client-server protocol using JSON-RPC {#} messages. The model still just emits tool calls; the MCP client forwards them.": "",
 "The host app runs one MCP client per server. Typical transports are local stdio and HTTP-based streaming.": "",
 "Security of Part II applies in full: an MCP server's tool descriptions and results are third-party text entering your context.": "",
